                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Payments.fs",
                "line": 17,
                "quote": "Accounts.coverage memberId library |> List.map (fun (_, covered) -> covered = PaidInFull)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "How payments are allocated is defined once, in Accounts.coverage. Payments.pay works out the settled fines by asking coverage before and after the payment, not by copying the allocation. Views.account uses the same function. The paid total is summed again in coverage the same way as in owed, in the same module, so the copies agree and cannot sensibly drift.",
