            "rationale": "The waiver rules all live in Tier 2: which fine can be waived, the approver being required, the fine no longer counting towards what is owed, and later payments skipping it (Waivers.waive, Fines.outstanding, Accounts.owed/coverage). The change also moves the borrowing-block rule out of the CLI and into Loans.borrow, which fixes an existing Tier 4 decision. One gap remains: for ordinary fines, Tier 2 classifies 'part paid' vs 'unpaid' (PaidInPart/Unpaid), but for waived fines Tier 3 Views makes that same distinction itself with 'paid > 0m'. That is a local re-derivation of part of the rule. It agrees with Tier 2 and does not contradict it.",
